title: The Party's Social Life
subtitle: Spend to keep the movement rooted when the factions are fighting.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_party_card
frequency: 170
view-if: month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_party_clubs_timer <= 0 and (internal_dissent >= 18 or party_unity < 45 or young_support < 50 or early_election_risk >= 25)
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_party_clubs_timer = 3
card-image: img/poland/cards/party-affairs.webp

= The Party's Social Life

The party has a parliamentary life and a social life. When the caucus is angry,
the members still need somewhere to meet, to play, to argue and to feel
belonging.

- @sports
- @youth_rooms
- @social_package
- @unify
- @nothing

@sports
title: Fund sports clubs and weekend activities
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Internal dissent falls and the party feels less brittle.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: A club programme needs one resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; internal_dissent -= 6; party_unity += 2; young_support += 2; local_network += 2; barons_dissent -= 1; spring_dissent -= 1; progressives_dissent -= 1; razem_dissent -= 1; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "Sports clubs help the party breathe again"

A few football matches, weekend trips and neighbourhood teams are not a substitute
for policy. They are, however, a way to keep members attached when the party
feels like it is only ever discussing itself.

- #poland_card_finish

@youth_rooms
title: Open youth rooms and local cultural spaces
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Local organising gains momentum.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Youth rooms require one resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; young_support += 3; local_network += 4; organiser_energy += 2; party_unity += 1; progressives_dissent -= 2; spring_dissent -= 1; news_headline = "Youth rooms become new organising hubs"

A rented hall, a library shelf and a regular meeting are enough to create a
second life for the party outside the press conference. The newcomers do not
always share the old guard's habits, which is the point.

- #poland_card_finish

@social_package
title: Expand small member benefits and mutual-aid work
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. The party looks useful, and the cost is visible later.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Another member benefit needs one resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; internal_dissent -= 4; public_trust += 1; party_unity += 1; budget_breaches += 1; barons_dissent -= 1; news_headline = "Member benefits soften the party's internal strain"

The party becomes less abstract. People who are not yet enthusiastic about a
programme can still feel the movement helping them through ordinary life.

- #poland_card_finish

@unify
title: Buy unity through a party weekend and public reassurance
subtitle: No resource cost, but the organisers give up their weekend to run it.
on-arrival: organiser_energy -= 3; internal_dissent -= 4; party_unity += 3; barons_dissent -= 1; spring_dissent -= 1; progressives_dissent -= 1; razem_dissent -= 1; social_patriot_dissent -= 1; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "The party buys a calmer mood with public reassurance"

The leadership turns the party into a place of reassurance for a weekend: a
rally, a speech, a shared meal, a visible reminder that the movement still
belongs to its members. The relief is real, even if it is temporary.

- #poland_card_finish

@nothing
title: Keep the party strictly electoral this month
subtitle: No immediate spend; the movement remains disciplined.
on-arrival: party_unity += 1; news_headline = "The party avoids a social spending programme"

The leadership decides that the caucus can survive one more month without
building clubs or member services.

- #poland_card_finish
